  "body": "## Complete counterexample at a fixed nonboundary rank\n\nFor the stationary binary Markov source with transition matrix ((3/4,1/4),(1/4,3/4)), the proof specifies one fixed rank proportion whose source coding has 1s at square positions. This rank is a continuity point of the first-order cost profile and is not a cylinder boundary.\n\nAlong an explicit deterministic sample-size subsequence, two positive-probability cost bands separate by much more than sqrt(n). Therefore the one-dimensional radix-selection cost is not tight under sqrt(n) scaling for **any deterministic centering**, including expectation centering. This gives a negative answer to universal fixed-rank marginal convergence in the original source model.\n\n## Independent validation\n\n- Separate adversarial review: PASS_COMPLETE_NONBOUNDARY_COUNTEREXAMPLE, no corrections\n- Frozen proof SHA-256: c72a38099e93b4d593be231e8f0c4ad726a399c3d61283da9f7b1f7e55801a5c\n- Review SHA-256: e3aa05eac01c81d82b869f206930fc70da1b73c205416c22ceec26ee6908263c\n- 16,642 submitted exact controls reproduce byte-for-byte; 44,602 independent controls pass\n- One substantive route, gpt-6-astra at xhigh; recommendation claimed_solved 1/5\n\nThe proof uses an elementary uniform cost bound and the binomial quantile CLT; finite controls support its identities rather than replace the asymptotic argument. The frozen manuscript's historical pending-review header is superseded by the completed review and current README/status.\n\n## Scope and attribution\n\nThe later Leckey\u2013Neininger\u2013Sulzbach paper already proves a dense boundary-rank obstruction; that result is credited. Its subsequent open-marginal sentence creates a source-scope tension retained in the audit. This construction addresses a nonboundary continuity rank instead. No almost-everywhere rank classification, claim about random centering, historical-priority claim, or human peer-review claim is made. Full original and author manuscripts were read; final publisher-typeset comparison was unavailable.\n\nAll files are isolated under attempts/30002720. Parent coordination will update the queue row. This is a review draft, not a merge or release.\n",
